    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>First-in-first-out work queue.</para><para>This simple work queue is meant to demonstrate the interface used by <ref refid="namespaceSawyer_1a1f34b997ec29ab29717d677098ff2b8c" kindref="member">processWorkList</ref>. New work is inserted at the back of the FIFO and consumed from the front. Only one type and three public member functions are necessary. The member functions must be thread safe if any of them are called from worker threads, otherwise they don&apos;t need to be thread safe since the <ref refid="namespaceSawyer_1a1f34b997ec29ab29717d677098ff2b8c" kindref="member">processWorkList</ref> will syncronize calls to this object. </para>    </detaileddescription>
